7.1 One level for all forms of a word
=====================================

By default each spelling has its own level.  To give a basic word and
all its forms one level:
     (setq bltzread-track-by 'lemma)
   This pairs well with writing to the word-families list:
     (setq bltzread-list-target 'word-families)


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Different list target per language,  Next: Skip the review,  Prev: One level for all forms of a word,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.2 Different list target per language
======================================

     (setq bltzread-list-target 'exact-words
           bltzread-list-target-alist '(("pli" . word-families)))


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Skip the review,  Next: Your own skip list files,  Prev: Different list target per language,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.3 Skip the review
===================

     (setq bltzread-known-write-policy 'immediate)
   Words reaching level 5 are written at once.  Careful: you can no
longer reject them.  The default is ‘unset’: it queues words like
‘review’ and warns once per session that you have not chosen.  Choose
‘review’ or ‘immediate’ and the warning goes away.


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Your own skip list files,  Next: Your own dictionary,  Prev: Skip the review,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.4 Your own skip list files
============================

     (setq bltzread-skip-exact-words-files
           '(("slv" . "~/lists/slv-words.txt")))
   Otherwise bltzread reads the paths from your bltzr settings file.


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Your own dictionary,  Next: A language that has no spaces,  Prev: Your own skip list files,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.5 Your own dictionary
=======================

Any function that takes a language and a list of words and returns text:
     (defun my-lookup (lang words)
       (shell-command-to-string
        (format "mydict %s %s" lang (car words))))
     (setq bltzread-dictionary-function #'my-lookup)


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: A language that has no spaces,  Next: Count repeated words,  Prev: Your own dictionary,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.6 A language that has no spaces
=================================

Give it its own word pattern:
     (setq bltzread-word-regexp-alist '(("xyz" . "[[:word:]]+")))


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Count repeated words,  Next: The card,  Prev: A language that has no spaces,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.7 Count repeated words
========================

     (setq bltzread-count-each-occurrence t)
   A word seen five times in the range gets five clean reads.


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: The card,  Next: Per-file language,  Prev: Count repeated words,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

7.8 The card
============

     (setq bltzread-popup-trigger 'manual     ; only when you press s .
           bltzread-popup-style 'side-window  ; never a floating box
           bltzread-popup-max-lines 12)


File: bltzread-tutorial.info,  Node: Per-file language,  Prev: The card,  Up: Part 6 Advanced options

